# Round 4 (review, 2026-07-27) removed the "reasoned-then-bare in old_string" case that
# used to sit here: measured to be killed only by the same mutant (m5_no_stale_check)
# that pre-existing case 74 already kills, and structurally UNABLE to discriminate
# search() from finditer() — when the reasoned marker is the FIRST occurrence in the
# string, .search() finds it exactly like finditer() would; there is no "reasoned-then-
# bare" construction where the two algorithms can ever disagree, by definition of what
# "first match" means. The discriminating order for old_string is bare-then-reasoned
# (the reason is NOT first) — already covered by the "FAIL-OPEN payload verbatim" case
# above. Dropped rather than "fixed" per the coordinator's instruction, since there is
# no version of this specific order that can be made to discriminate.
{"desc": "no-silent-removal: bare-then-reasoned marker order in new_string (a genuine reason present, but NOT the first occurrence) must still pass — a real justification must not be ignored because a bare marker sits above it", "hook": "plugins/core/hooks/no-silent-removal.sh", "input": {"tool_name": "Edit", "tool_input": {"file_path": "/tmp/x.dart", "old_string": "@injectable\nclass Foo {}", "new_string": "// agent-kit: removal intentional\n// agent-kit: removal intentional — parent constructs it now\nclass Foo {}"}}, "expect_exit": 0}
{"desc": "no-silent-removal: reasoned-then-bare marker order in new_string (reason IS the first occurrence this time) — same genuine-justification case, order must not matter, still passes", "hook": "plugins/core/hooks/no-silent-removal.sh", "input": {"tool_name": "Edit", "tool_input": {"file_path": "/tmp/x.dart", "old_string": "@injectable\nclass Foo {}", "new_string": "// agent-kit: removal intentional — Foo is constructed by the parent now\n// agent-kit: removal intentional\nclass Foo {}"}}, "expect_exit": 0}
