# --- citation-check (core, 2026-07-27): moves citation validation from skill-invoked to event-driven ---
# Fix round 1 (review, 2026-07-27): the original 4 cases pinned almost nothing -- 3 pointed at
# files run-evals.sh never creates, so they exited 0 through the isfile(fp) guard without ever
# reaching the gate they were named after (root cause quoted in CHANGELOG.md). Replaced with a
# set where each case exercises the exact dimension it names, against a fixture that exists.
#
# Fix round 3 (review, 2026-07-27): the hook now matches the CONTAINING DIRECTORY, not the
# basename alone -- a write is the kit's artifact only when its parent directory is
# `agent-kit-findings`, the namespace both producers write into. The fixtures moved to mirror
# that: evals/fixtures/citation-check/agent-kit-findings/*.findings.json is the kit's side of
# the boundary, evals/fixtures/citation-check/foreign/ is the other side, holding the same
# content under the same watched names. Every case below that carries a path in its PAYLOAD
# TEXT rather than a fixture (the I3 guard cases) had to be rewritten too: the bash pre-filter
# now screens on `agent-kit-findings`, so a payload carrying only `findings.json` is declined
# before python runs and the case pins nothing. Each one was mutation-tested individually.
# Ledger fixtures: a real ledger for "cc-real-session" (covers some/fake/verified.dart:10-20,
# NOT some/fake/bar.dart) plus a newer "decoy" ledger for "cc-decoy-session" (covers bar.dart)
# and an empty ledger for "cc-empty-ledger-session" -- all created in run-evals.sh's fixture
# section (mtime control).
{"desc": "citation-check: a Write whose raw payload cannot contain a path in the kit's findings directory is declined by the bash pre-filter, before a python3 interpreter is ever forked", "hook": "plugins/core/hooks/citation-check.sh", "input": {"tool_name": "Write", "tool_input": {"file_path": "{{TMPDIR}}/agent-kit-evals/notes.md", "content": "hello"}}, "expect_exit": 0}
{"desc": "citation-check: ignores non-Write tools (path inside the kit's directory so the bash pre-filter passes it through to the tool_name check)", "hook": "plugins/core/hooks/citation-check.sh", "input": {"tool_name": "Read", "tool_input": {"file_path": "{{TMPDIR}}/agent-kit-evals/agent-kit-findings/findings.json"}}, "expect_exit": 0}
{"desc": "citation-check: ignores non-Write tools even on a REAL fabricated findings file in the kit's own directory that would otherwise gate-trip (kills the tool_name-guard-deleted mutant)", "hook": "plugins/core/hooks/citation-check.sh", "env": {"CLAUDE_PLUGIN_DATA": "{{TMPDIR}}/agent-kit-evals/citation-check-data"}, "input": {"tool_name": "Read", "session_id": "cc-real-session", "tool_input": {"file_path": "{{REPO_ROOT}}/evals/fixtures/citation-check/agent-kit-findings/fabricated.findings.json"}}, "expect_exit": 0}
{"desc": "citation-check: ignores a non-canonical basename INSIDE the kit's own directory, on a REAL file with fabricated content that would otherwise gate-trip (kills the basename-guard-deleted mutant). The fixture sits in agent-kit-findings/ ON PURPOSE: the directory test passes, so the case reaches the basename test it is named after instead of being declined one line earlier -- the boundary rule and the naming rule are two separate guards and each needs its own killer", "hook": "plugins/core/hooks/citation-check.sh", "env": {"CLAUDE_PLUGIN_DATA": "{{TMPDIR}}/agent-kit-evals/citation-check-data"}, "input": {"tool_name": "Write", "session_id": "cc-real-session", "tool_input": {"file_path": "{{REPO_ROOT}}/evals/fixtures/citation-check/agent-kit-findings/fabricated.findings.json.md"}}, "expect_exit": 0}
{"desc": "citation-check: a genuinely verified citation against the real ledger silences (kills a weakened/inverted gate-exit-code check)", "hook": "plugins/core/hooks/citation-check.sh", "env": {"CLAUDE_PLUGIN_DATA": "{{TMPDIR}}/agent-kit-evals/citation-check-data"}, "input": {"tool_name": "Write", "session_id": "cc-real-session", "tool_input": {"file_path": "{{REPO_ROOT}}/evals/fixtures/citation-check/agent-kit-findings/verified.findings.json"}}, "expect_exit": 0}
{"desc": "citation-check: a fabricated citation against a real (non-covering) ledger blocks with exit 2 and the report lands on STDERR -- the one exit code on which Claude Code feeds stderr back to the model, and the reason the gate report does not use the additionalContext envelope the fail-open notices do. The needle is a line the validator prints on ITS stdout, so the case also kills the stdout-dropped-from-report mutant (the hook merges r.stdout+r.stderr before forwarding), alongside the exit-code-propagation mutant", "hook": "plugins/core/hooks/citation-check.sh", "env": {"CLAUDE_PLUGIN_DATA": "{{TMPDIR}}/agent-kit-evals/citation-check-data"}, "input": {"tool_name": "Write", "session_id": "cc-real-session", "tool_input": {"file_path": "{{REPO_ROOT}}/evals/fixtures/citation-check/agent-kit-findings/fabricated.findings.json"}}, "expect_exit": 2, "expect_stderr_contains": "file/range never read this session"}
{"desc": "citation-check: a path inside the kit's directory with a matching name but absent from disk short-circuits silently, never invoking the validator (kills the isfile(fp)-guard-deleted mutant). expect_not_contains asserts TOTAL silence via the notice prefix every fail-open message carries, not the wording of any one message", "hook": "plugins/core/hooks/citation-check.sh", "env": {"CLAUDE_PLUGIN_DATA": "{{TMPDIR}}/agent-kit-evals/citation-check-data"}, "input": {"tool_name": "Write", "session_id": "cc-real-session", "tool_input": {"file_path": "{{TMPDIR}}/agent-kit-evals/citation-check-data/agent-kit-findings/ghost.findings.json"}}, "expect_exit": 0, "expect_not_contains": "[citation-check]"}
{"desc": "citation-check: no session_id in the event skips with a visible notice rather than risking a false clear via auto-discovery's decoy ledger (I6/R6) -- a genuinely fabricated citation must NOT come back verified just because a newer, unrelated session's ledger happens to cover it. Asserted on STDOUT, not the merged stream: an exit-0 hook's stderr never reaches the model, so a notice that only lands there is a false clear dressed as a warning", "hook": "plugins/core/hooks/citation-check.sh", "env": {"CLAUDE_PLUGIN_DATA": "{{TMPDIR}}/agent-kit-evals/citation-check-data"}, "input": {"tool_name": "Write", "tool_input": {"file_path": "{{REPO_ROOT}}/evals/fixtures/citation-check/agent-kit-findings/fabricated.findings.json"}}, "expect_exit": 0, "expect_stdout_contains": "no session_id in this event"}
{"desc": "citation-check: session_id present but no ledger file exists for it at all skips with a MODEL-VISIBLE notice, not a fabrication report (I6/R6). This case pins the ENVELOPE, not the wording: expect_stdout_contains looks for hookSpecificOutput, which is what makes stdout reach the model at all -- a mutant that drops the envelope and prints the same sentence as bare stdout text would satisfy a needle-only assertion while being exactly as invisible as the stderr bug this replaced", "hook": "plugins/core/hooks/citation-check.sh", "env": {"CLAUDE_PLUGIN_DATA": "{{TMPDIR}}/agent-kit-evals/citation-check-data"}, "input": {"tool_name": "Write", "session_id": "cc-nonexistent-session", "tool_input": {"file_path": "{{REPO_ROOT}}/evals/fixtures/citation-check/agent-kit-findings/verified.findings.json"}}, "expect_exit": 0, "expect_stdout_contains": "hookSpecificOutput", "expect_contains": "no usable read-ledger"}
{"desc": "citation-check: session_id present but its ledger file is empty (0 bytes) skips with a MODEL-VISIBLE notice, not a fabrication report (I6/R6) -- the needle asserted on stdout specifically, the counterpart to the envelope pin on the case above", "hook": "plugins/core/hooks/citation-check.sh", "env": {"CLAUDE_PLUGIN_DATA": "{{TMPDIR}}/agent-kit-evals/citation-check-data"}, "input": {"tool_name": "Write", "session_id": "cc-empty-ledger-session", "tool_input": {"file_path": "{{REPO_ROOT}}/evals/fixtures/citation-check/agent-kit-findings/verified.findings.json"}}, "expect_exit": 0, "expect_stdout_contains": "no usable read-ledger"}
{"desc": "citation-check: a session_id that is not a string (a list) is coerced to absent and skips with the MODEL-VISIBLE no-session notice, never a TypeError (New-2 -- kills the isinstance(session, str) guard mutant: without it, a truthy non-string sails past `if not session` into the ledger-path concat and crashes the hook to exit 1)", "hook": "plugins/core/hooks/citation-check.sh", "env": {"CLAUDE_PLUGIN_DATA": "{{TMPDIR}}/agent-kit-evals/citation-check-data"}, "input": {"tool_name": "Write", "session_id": ["cc-real-session"], "tool_input": {"file_path": "{{REPO_ROOT}}/evals/fixtures/citation-check/agent-kit-findings/verified.findings.json"}}, "expect_exit": 0, "expect_stdout_contains": "no session_id in this event"}
