# --- fix round 3 (review, 2026-07-27): the directory boundary itself ---
# citation-check.sh ships at USER scope: it fires on every Write in every project. Matching
# the basename alone claimed any findings.json anywhere, including foreign tools' output --
# an eslint-shaped array of {filePath, messages} reached --gate and was BLOCKED at exit 2
# as fabrication, and apk-archaeology's top-level object injected "treat every citation as
# unconfirmed" into sessions that had no citations. The four cases below hold the same
# content under the same watched names in a NON-kit directory and require total silence.
# Every one of them fails if the match is widened back to the basename: verified by applying
# that exact widening (both the bash pre-filter and the python parent-directory test) and
# watching them die -- see task-8-report.md for which case died on which mutant.
{"desc": "citation-check BOUNDARY: a foreign findings.json whose content is a valid findings array with a fabricated citation -- the exact file that the basename-only rule BLOCKED at exit 2 -- is not ours and gets silence. This is the primary widening-mutation killer", "hook": "plugins/core/hooks/citation-check.sh", "env": {"CLAUDE_PLUGIN_DATA": "{{TMPDIR}}/agent-kit-evals/citation-check-data"}, "input": {"tool_name": "Write", "session_id": "cc-real-session", "tool_input": {"file_path": "{{REPO_ROOT}}/evals/fixtures/citation-check/foreign/findings.json"}}, "expect_exit": 0, "expect_not_contains": "[citation-check]"}
{"desc": "citation-check BOUNDARY: an eslint-shaped array ([{filePath, messages}]) at a watched name outside the kit's directory exits 0 SILENTLY. Under the basename-only rule this exited 2: the validator read the array as one finding with no evidence and the hook hard-blocked a foreign tool's write as fabricated", "hook": "plugins/core/hooks/citation-check.sh", "env": {"CLAUDE_PLUGIN_DATA": "{{TMPDIR}}/agent-kit-evals/citation-check-data"}, "input": {"tool_name": "Write", "session_id": "cc-real-session", "tool_input": {"file_path": "{{REPO_ROOT}}/evals/fixtures/citation-check/foreign/eslint.findings.json"}}, "expect_exit": 0, "expect_not_contains": "[citation-check]"}
{"desc": "citation-check BOUNDARY: apk-archaeology's own emitter shape (a top-level object with capabilities) at a watched name outside the kit's directory exits 0 SILENTLY -- no context injection. Under the basename-only rule this injected a validator error and an instruction to distrust citations into a session that had none", "hook": "plugins/core/hooks/citation-check.sh", "env": {"CLAUDE_PLUGIN_DATA": "{{TMPDIR}}/agent-kit-evals/citation-check-data"}, "input": {"tool_name": "Write", "session_id": "cc-real-session", "tool_input": {"file_path": "{{REPO_ROOT}}/evals/fixtures/citation-check/foreign/apk-capabilities.findings.json"}}, "expect_exit": 0, "expect_not_contains": "[citation-check]"}
{"desc": "citation-check BOUNDARY: a directory whose name merely CONTAINS agent-kit-findings is not the kit's directory -- the bash pre-filter (a substring test) passes this through and python's parent-component test, which is an EQUALITY, declines it. Kills a mutant that relaxes python's test to the same substring match the pre-filter uses", "hook": "plugins/core/hooks/citation-check.sh", "env": {"CLAUDE_PLUGIN_DATA": "{{TMPDIR}}/agent-kit-evals/citation-check-data"}, "input": {"tool_name": "Write", "session_id": "cc-real-session", "tool_input": {"file_path": "{{TMPDIR}}/agent-kit-evals/agent-kit-findings-backup/fabricated.findings.json"}}, "expect_exit": 0, "expect_not_contains": "[citation-check]"}
# The three path-normalization cases. normpath runs before the parent-component test, so a
# path is judged by where it LANDS, not by how it was spelled.
{"desc": "citation-check: a path that passes THROUGH the kit's directory but resolves out of it (.. traversal) is declined. This is the pre-filter's cannot-disagree invariant in its only interesting direction: the raw payload carries the agent-kit-findings substring so the bash guard passes it through, and python -- the authoritative test -- declines after normalization. The guard is allowed to be looser; python accepting what the guard declined is what must never happen", "hook": "plugins/core/hooks/citation-check.sh", "env": {"CLAUDE_PLUGIN_DATA": "{{TMPDIR}}/agent-kit-evals/citation-check-data"}, "input": {"tool_name": "Write", "session_id": "cc-real-session", "tool_input": {"file_path": "{{REPO_ROOT}}/evals/fixtures/citation-check/agent-kit-findings/../foreign/findings.json"}}, "expect_exit": 0, "expect_not_contains": "[citation-check]"}
{"desc": "citation-check: a `.` segment between the kit's directory and the filename still resolves INTO the directory and still gates (kills the normpath-deleted mutant: os.path.dirname on the un-normalized path returns \".\", the parent component reads as \".\", and the kit's own artifact gets declined). Measured, not assumed -- this is the one form among the four checked where raw and normalized parents actually differ; the macOS double slash is NOT, os.path.dirname collapses redundant separators by itself", "hook": "plugins/core/hooks/citation-check.sh", "env": {"CLAUDE_PLUGIN_DATA": "{{TMPDIR}}/agent-kit-evals/citation-check-data"}, "input": {"tool_name": "Write", "session_id": "cc-real-session", "tool_input": {"file_path": "{{REPO_ROOT}}/evals/fixtures/citation-check/agent-kit-findings/./fabricated.findings.json"}}, "expect_exit": 2, "expect_stderr_contains": "file/range never read this session"}
{"desc": "citation-check: the double slash the producers' path actually renders with on macOS (TMPDIR ends in a separator, so ${TMPDIR:-/tmp}/agent-kit-findings/ becomes .../T//agent-kit-findings/) still gates. Pins the real-world path shape end to end rather than the idealized one every other case uses", "hook": "plugins/core/hooks/citation-check.sh", "env": {"CLAUDE_PLUGIN_DATA": "{{TMPDIR}}/agent-kit-evals/citation-check-data"}, "input": {"tool_name": "Write", "session_id": "cc-real-session", "tool_input": {"file_path": "{{REPO_ROOT}}/evals/fixtures/citation-check//agent-kit-findings/fabricated.findings.json"}}, "expect_exit": 2, "expect_stderr_contains": "file/range never read this session"}
